en_ids}`, MD5 ids, stored as\none JSON file each under `~/.memoray/data/entities/`. Overview agent split keys off `agent.toLowerCase()`.\n\n**Phase 1 DONE — opencode audited in memo-ray.** Added `parsers/opencodeParser.js` (+ config/detector/\ncapabilities/overview/SetupWizard/OverviewGrid). opencode stores JSON-per-entity under\n`~/.local/share/opencode/storage/` (project→session→message→part; tool parts hold both call `state.input`\nand result `state.output`); config+permissions at `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`. Parser uses\n`agent: 'Opencode'`, falls back to default paths when the user's generated config predates the OPENCODE_* keys.\nVerified: 4 real sessions → 87 entities; capabilities returns providers/models/MCP/permissions; client builds.\nTakes effect on next memo-ray restart (boot-sync ingests into real ~/.memoray/data).\n\n**Phase 2 DONE — open-notebook ingested + audited in memo-ray.** Runs via docker-compose at\n`C:\\Users\\nsdha\\docker-compose.yml` (open_notebook Web UI :8502, REST API :5055; surrealdb :8000\nroot/root, ns+db `open_notebook`; encryption key hardcoded `benny` — make per-install in Phase 5).\nThe compose failure the user hit was just Docker Desktop's engine not running. Added\n`parsers/openNotebookParser.js` — an **API client** (not file parser), Node global `fetch`, bounded\ntimeouts: GET /api/notebooks → Session, /api/sources?notebook_id → Artifact, /api/notes?notebook_id →\nThought(ai)/Message(human); agent `OpenNotebook`; stable ids `hash('opennotebook:...')`; skips quietly\nif API down. Config key `OPEN_NOTEBOOK_API_URL` (default http://localhost:5055, env MEMORAY_OPEN_NOTEBOOK_URL;\nit's a URL not a path so it bypasses the detector). Capabilities `openNotebook` block audits providers\n(available/configured), models, **transformations = the AI operations** (6 seeded), encryption. Overview adds\n`opennotebook` agent key. OverviewGrid has an open-notebook column. Verified: notebook+note → Session+Thought;\ncapabilities returns the 6 transformations. KNOWN REFINEMENT: list endpoints return note `content`=null\n(content only in GET /api/notes/{id}); sources' full_text may also need detail fetch — fine for lineage/audit,\nrevisit when feeding Benny RAG.\n\n**Next:** Phase 2b feed open-notebook sources into Benny RAG (`/api/runtime/rag/ingest`); Phase 3 opencode as a\nBenny execution backend; Phase 4 floating dog; Phase 5 unified packaging/tray/release (+ per-install encryption key).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":5,"newStart":46,"newLines":18,"lines":[" (content only in GET /api/notes/{id}); sources' full_text may also need detail fetch — fine for lineage/audit,"," revisit when feeding Benny RAG."," ","-**Next:** Phase 2b feed open-notebook sources into Benny RAG (`/api/runtime/rag/ingest`); Phase 3 opencode as a","-Benny execution backend; Phase 4 floating dog; Phase 5 unified packaging/tray/release (+ per-install encryption key).","+**Phase 4a DONE — Benny floating overlay reskinned to a dog.** The floating overlay lives at","+`prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_core/onscreen_agent/` (draggable avatar, edge-hide peeking, compact/full).","+Avatar art was an astronaut webp in shared `_core/visual/res/chat/overlay/`. Authored two new SVGs there —","+`dog_no_bg.svg` (floating draggable avatar, square 256 viewBox, centered/shadowless so edge-hide poses match)","+and `dog_head_256.svg` (in-chat assistant avatar) — a friendly Shiba \"Benny\". Repointed `panel.html` (avatar img","+src, was `astronaut_no_bg.webp`) and `view.js` (`assistantAvatarPath`, was `helmet_no_bg_256.webp`); left the","+astronaut/helmet assets intact for other surfaces. CSS uses object-fit:contain on a square cluster + float anim +","+scaleX flip on right edge + rotate on edge-hide, so the SVG drops in. Updated the module's AGENTS.md (doc-first","+contract) asset-naming lines + a note that legacy \"astronaut\" wording = the same dog avatar. NOT yet verified in","+the running prime-silo app (needs `node space serve`);