fest\nnode type in `api/studio_executor.py` (dispatches trigger/llm/data/logic), add explicit HITL approval node for mutations.\n\n**Next:** user tests 2b ingest + 3 live run with Benny running; Phase 5 unified packaging/tray/release\n(+ per-install open-notebook encryption key, bundle opencode serve + open-notebook beside Benny runtime). All\nphase playbooks are in the shareable `prime-silo/OPEN-STUDIO.md`.","originalFile":"---\nname: project-open-studio-opencode-audit\ndescription: Open-Studio project — folding opencode + open-notebook into memo-ray + Benny; Phase 1 (opencode audited in memo-ray) is done\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: c9e03e56-5425-4e3d-8d0c-40d1a1b8d58d\n---\n\n**Open-Studio** is a project (started 2026-06-19) to fold two OSS tools into the existing\nbinary16 stack instead of building those slices from scratch: **opencode** (sst/opencode,\nlocal coding agent) and **open-notebook** (lfnovo, open NotebookLM). Plan file:\n`~/.claude/plans/i-was-thinking-of-hazy-platypus.md`. Decisions: extend memo-ray + prime-silo\nin place (no new repo); make memo-ray the universal local-agent audit layer; make Benny a\nfloating \"dog\" (phased: reskin the in-browser `_core/onscreen_agent/` overlay → standalone\nalways-on-top desktop-pet window). See [[project-binary16-app-registry]], [[benny-self-awareness-and-bridge-files]].\n\n**memo-ray audit pattern** (how Claude/Gemini are \"audited\" — and now opencode too): four seams in\n`memo-ray/agent-os-dashboard/server`: (1) `memoray.config.js` paths (but the *runtime* config is\nthe auto-generated `~/.memoray/memoray.config.js` from `lib/config.js`+`lib/detector.js`, NOT the\nrepo file); (2) `lib/detector.js` PROBE_LISTS/GUIDES + singleKeys/arrayKeys; (3) `parsers/<agent>Parser.js`\n→ entities; (4) `/api/system/capabilities` reads each agent's tools/permission grants = the audit.\nEntities: `{id,type,agent,timestamp,content,metadata,parent_id,children_ids}`, MD5 ids, stored as\none JSON file each under `~/.memoray/data/entities/`. Overview agent split keys off `agent.toLowerCase()`.\n\n**Phase 1 DONE — opencode audited in memo-ray.** Added `parsers/opencodeParser.js` (+ config/detector/\ncapabilities/overview/SetupWizard/OverviewGrid). opencode stores JSON-per-entity under\n`~/.local/share/opencode/storage/` (project→session→message→part; tool parts hold both call `state.input`\nand result `state.output`); config+permissions at `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json`. Parser uses\n`agent: 'Opencode'`, falls back to default paths when the user's generated config predates the OPENCODE_* keys.\nVerified: 4 real sessions → 87 entities; capabilities returns providers/models/MCP/permissions; client builds.\nTakes effect on next memo-ray restart (boot-sync ingests into real ~/.memoray/data).\n\n**Phase 2 DONE — open-notebook ingested + audited in memo-ray.** Runs via docker-compose at\n`C:\\Users\\nsdha\\docker-compose.yml` (open_notebook Web UI :8502, REST API :5055; surrealdb :8000\nroot/root, ns+db `open_notebook`; encryption key hardcoded `benny` — make per-install in Phase 5).\nThe compose failure the user hit was just Docker Desktop's engine not running. Added\n`parsers/openNotebookParser.js` — an **API client** (not file parser), Node global `fetch`, bounded\ntimeouts: GET /api/notebooks → Session, /api/sources?notebook_id → Artifact, /api/notes?notebook_id →\nThought(ai)/Message(human); agent `OpenNotebook`; stable ids `hash('opennotebook:...')`; skips quietly\nif API down. Config key `OPEN_NOTEBOOK_API_URL` (default http://localhost:5055, env MEMORAY_OPEN_NOTEBOOK_URL;\nit's a URL not a path so it bypasses the detector). Capabilities `openNotebook` block audits providers\n(available/configured), models, **transformations = the AI operations** (6 seeded), encryption. Overview adds\n`opennotebook` agent key. OverviewGrid has an open-notebook column. Verified: notebook+note → Session+Thought;\ncapabilities returns the 6 transformations. KNOWN REFINEMENT: list endpoints return note `content`=null\n(content only in GET /api/notes/{id}); sources' full_text may also need detail fetch — fine for lineage/audit,\nrevisit when feeding Benny RAG.\n\n**Phase 4a DONE — Benny floating overlay reskinned to a dog.** The floating overlay lives at\n`prime-silo/app/L0/_all/mod/_core/onscreen_agent/` (draggable avatar, edge-hide peeking, compact/full).\nAvatar art was an astronaut webp in shared `_core/visual/res/chat/overlay/`. Authored two new SVGs there —\n`dog_no_bg.svg` (floating draggable avatar, square 256 viewBox, centered/shadowless so edge-hide poses match)\nand `dog_head_256.svg` (in-chat assistant avatar) — a friendly Shiba \"Benny\". Repointed `panel.html` (avatar img\nsrc, was `astronaut_no_bg.webp`) and `view.js` (`assistantAvatarPath`, was `helmet_no_bg_256.webp`); left the\nastronaut/helmet assets intact for other surfaces. CSS uses object-fit:contain on a square cluster + float anim +\nscaleX flip on right edge + rotate on edge-hide, so the SVG drops in. Updated the module's AGENTS.md (doc-first\ncontract) asset-naming lines + a note that legacy \"astronaut\" wording = the same dog avatar. NOT yet verified in\nthe running prime-silo app (needs `node space serve`); verified via rendered pose mockup only.\n\nBenny breed: user chose **German Shepherd** (tan + black saddle, big erect ears, black mask/muzzle, brow dots) —\nboth `dog_no_bg.svg` and `dog_head_256.svg` are now GSD.\n\n**Phase 4b DONE — standalone desktop-pet window.** New `prime-silo/packaging/desktop/pet.js` (frameless,\ntransparent, alwaysOnTop \"screen-saver\", skipTaskbar BrowserWindow, bottom-right of work area; create/destroy/toggle\n+ ipcMain `space-desktop:pet-open-cockpit`/`pet-hide`), `pet-preload.js` (contextBridge `window.benny.openCockpit/hide`),\n`pet.html` (transparent, GSD inlined + `-webkit-app-region: drag`, hover chat-paw + close controls, soft drop-shadow).\nWired in `main.js`: required the module, added `togglePet`/`isPetVisible` to the tray options (chat paw → showMainWindow+createWindow),\n`destroyDesktopPet()` in `prepareDesktopForQuit()`. `tray.js` `buildMenu` has a \"Show Benny on desktop\"/\"Hide Benny (desktop pet)\"\ntoggle. electron-builder `build.files` already globs `packaging/desktop/**/*` so the 3 new files bundle automatically.\nAll 4 desktop files pass `node --check`; pet.html renders. NOT run in a live Electron build (needs full desktop build);\nverified via syntax + rendered mock only.\n\n**SHAREABLE HANDOVER NOW IN REPO: `prime-silo/OPEN-STUDIO.md`** — full phased plan + status table + per-phase\nplaybooks + architecture coordinates, written so a lesser/cheaper agent can execute a single phase cold (user is\nlimit-constrained and wants to hand off). Keep its Status table updated when phases land. This private memory is the\nauthor's copy; OPEN-STUDIO.md is the shareable one.\n\n**Phase 2b DONE (export) — bridge `prime-silo/scripts/openstudio-notebook-bridge.mjs`.** KEY FACT: Benny\n`runtime/benny/api/rag_routes.py :: POST /rag/ingest` ingests FILES from `$BENNY_HOME/workspaces/<ws>/data_in/`\n(body = `{workspace, files?, deep_synthesis, force_reingest,...}`), NOT raw text. So the bridge: (A) GET open-notebook\nnotebooks→sources (5055), resolve each source's full text (full_text → `/api/sources/{id}` → `/api/sources/{id}/download`),\nwrite `data_in/<notebook>__<title>.md`; (B) unless `--no-ingest`, POST ingest (default `http://localhost:3000/api/runtime/rag/ingest`,\nheader `X-Benny-API-Key: benny-mesh-2026-auth`, `{workspace, deep_synthesis:true, force_reingest:true}`). No deps (global fetch).\nEnv/flags: OPEN_NOTEBOOK_URL/--notebook-url, BENNY_DATA_IN/--data-in (required), BENNY_INGEST_URL/--ingest-url,\nBENNY_API_KEY, BENNY_WORKSPACE, --notebook <id>, --no-ingest. Verified export e2e vs a mock (wrote correct .md);\nclean error when open-notebook unreachable. Ingest POST untested — needs live Benny runtime (user will test).\nNOTE: Docker engine keeps crashing on this machine; open-notebook (compose at C:\\Users\\nsdha\\docker-compose.yml) was down at test time.\n\n**Next:** user tests 2b ingest with Benny running; Phase 3 opencode as Benny execution backend (adapter near\n`runtime/benny/graph/swarm.py`, behind HITL/ADR-001); Phase 5 unified packaging/tray/release (+ per-install ON encryption key).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":86,"oldLines":5,"newStart":86,"newLines":18,"lines":[" clean error when open-notebook unreachable. Ingest POST untested — needs live Benny runtime (user will test)."," NOTE: Docker engine keeps crashing on this machine; open-notebook (compose at C:\\Users\\nsdha\\docker-compose.yml) was down at test time."," ","-**Next:** user tests 2b ingest with Benny running; Phase 3 opencode as Benny execution backend (adapter near","-`runtime/benny/graph/swarm.py`, behind HITL/ADR-001); Phase 5 unified packaging/tray/release (+ per-install ON encryption key).","+**Phase 3 DONE (built, live run untested) — opencode as a Benny execution backend.** Added","+`prime-silo/runtime/benny/tools/opencode.py` (stdlib-only: `opencode_available()` + async","+`run_opencode_task(prompt,cwd,model?,agent?,timeout?)` → runs `opencode run <prompt> [-m provider/model]`","+headless via asyncio subprocess, captures stdout/stderr/returncode + git diff/changed_files) and","+`runtime/benny/api/opencode_routes.py` (`GET /api/opencode/status`, `POST /api/opencode/run`","+{prompt,workspace,subdir?,model?,agent?,timeout?}; confines to workspace root per ADR-001, TaskManager +","+lineage track start/complete/fail). Registered in `runtime/benny/api/server.py` (import + include_router","+prefix `/api/opencode`). opencode CLI confirmed: `opencode run [msg] -m provider/model --agent --format json`.","+Verified: py_compile all 3 + server.py OK; opencode_available()=True; subprocess capture works (git --version).","+Live coding run untested (needs Benny runtime + ollama; would be slow). Follow-ups: wire as a swarm/manifest","+node type in `api/studio_executor.py` (dispatches trigger/llm/data/logic), add explicit HITL approval node for mutations.","+","+**Next:** user tests 2b ingest + 3 live run with Benny running; Phase 5 unified packaging/tray/release","+(+ per-install open-notebook encryption key, bundle opencode serve + open-notebook beside Benny runtime). All","+phase playbooks are in the shareable `prime-silo/OPEN-STUDIO.md`."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d75509d-376a-4a14-9647-15174b2f8a6f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\Users\\nsdha\\OneDrive\\binary16\\prime-silo\\runtime\\benny","sessionId":"c9e03e56-5425-4e3d-8d0c-40d1a1b8d58d","version":"2.1.181","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"i-was-thinking-of-hazy-platypus"}
